title: D1_00_Start
---
// ================================================================
// DEMO_3Days.yarn — the three-day demo (Bar 410).
//   Day 1  Walter, Isla, Owen     (start node D1_00_Start)
//   Day 2  Walter, Cole, Eliana   (start node D2_00_Start)
//   Day 3  Faye, Isla, Arthur, Owen (start node D3_00_Start, at most 3 in the bar at once)
// Day 1 was Day1_Demo.yarn; days 2-3 come from the team's script
// bar_script_day2_day3 (Freya is called Faye in the game).
//
// Run: the Day Schedule on [GameLoop] › FlowWiring (DaySchedule_Demo) lists the
// three start nodes. Same shape as PLAYTEST_Demo.yarn:
//   BeforeOpen  : the day's popups (new ingredients, from IngredientUnlockTable), then the start node.
//                 <<flow_open_bar>> opens the bar and waits for the chapter title.
//   Open        : order -> <<flow_prepare_drinks>> -> <<wait_for_task>> -> reaction
//                 -> <<Reset_Variable>>.
//   end of day  : <<flow_close_bar>> ... <<flow_next_day>> as the very last command.
// Orders whose name is not spoken are placed with <<set $order_note = ...>>.
// Customer numbers for Order_Cocktail_OutName: Cole 1, Owen 2, Walter 3, Faye 4,
// Isla 5, Claire 6, Eliana 7, Arthur 8.
// ================================================================

<<enum TypeOfCocktail>>
    <<case None>>
    <<case HighAlcohol>>
    <<case LowAlcohol>>
    <<case NoneAlcohol>>
    <<case NotMatch>>
<<endenum>>
<<enum Satisfaction>>
    <<case None>>
    <<case Fail>>
    <<case Acceptable>>
    <<case Perfect>>
<<endenum>>
<<enum CharacterName>>
    <<case None>>
    <<case Cole>>
    <<case Owen>>
    <<case Walter>>
    <<case Faye>>
    <<case Isla>>
    <<case Claire>>
    <<case Eliana>>
    <<case Arthur>>
<<endenum>>
// Declare the variable (set false by default)
<<declare $type_of_cocktail = TypeOfCocktail.None>>
<<declare $satisfaction = Satisfaction.None>>
// Day number. C# (FlowWiring) picks each day's start node from SO_DaySchedule by this.
<<declare $day = 1>>
// Holds the name of an order the customer does not say out loud.
<<declare $order_note = "">>

<<eventlog_clear>>
<<flow_open_bar>>
<<jump D1_01_Walter_Arrive>>
===

title: D1_01_Walter_Arrive
---
<<Walter Enter 1>>
<<Switch_Camera CamController Char1Cam>>
<<Walter Happy>>


//Walter greeting
Walter: Good evening.[waitfor=0.2/] It's been a long time since I last saw someone open something new in this town. #line:0
Walter: You must be the new face in town. #line:1
-> Welcome #line:2
    Player: Good evening, welcome to the bar. #line:3
    Player: Please, take your time and make yourself comfortable. #line:4
-> Honest #line:5
    Player: Yes, I just opened tonight. #line:6
    Player: Still trying to get used to how quiet this town is. #line:7
-> Friendly #line:8
    Player: Really? I thought I've been running this place since the 20th century. #line:9
    Walter: [wiggle]Haha... quite a talker.[/wiggle] #line:A
-> Formal #line:B
    Player: Welcome. It's a pleasure to have you as my first guest. #line:C

Walter: I'm Walter, by the way. #line:D
Player: Nice to meet you Mr. Walter. #line:E
Player: You can call me bartender. #line:F
Walter: Normally at this hour, I'd just be sitting in front of the TV. #line:10
Walter: [dangle]Old habits, I suppose.[/dangle] #line:11
Walter: But I saw a new place opening up, so I thought I'd drop by. #line:12
Walter: Wanted to see the new face in town for myself. #line:13
Player: Well, glad I opened the doors tonight. #line:14
Player: I'm sure this place will be better than TV. #line:15
Player: So, what will it be tonight? #line:16
<<jump D1_02_Walter_Order>>

===

title: D1_02_Walter_Order
---
//Walter's Order
Walter: Just keep it simple, son. #line:17
<<order_customer "[CocktailSystem]" Walter>>
Walter: [order] "{Order_Cocktail_ByName_OutName("Sea Breeze")}" [/order] should be enough for tonight. #line:18
Player: Coming right up. #line:19
<<Owen Neutral>>

<<flow_prepare_drinks>>

<<wait_for_task SystemGame>>

//After Walter's order
<<Switch_Camera CamController Char1Cam>>

<<if $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Perfect>>
    <<Walter Happy>>
    Walter: [bounce]Spot on, son.[/bounce] #line:1A
    Walter: [wave]Balanced and clean.[/wave] You've got a steady hand for a new face. #line:1B
    Player: Thank you. #line:1C
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Acceptable>>
    Walter: A bit off, but it's alright. #line:1D
<<elseif $satisfaction == Satisfaction.Fail>>
    <<Walter Sad>>
    Walter: [shake]I don't think this is what I asked for.[/shake] #line:1E
    Walter: [wiggle]My memory might be fading, but my tongue still works.[/wiggle] #line:1F
<<endif>>

<<Reset_Variable SystemGame>>

<<Walter Neutral>>
<<jump D1_03_Walter_Talk>>
===

